+Prop.4.4, pp.168--169, is a conditional nonsplitting theorem: after seven
+hypotheses it concludes that the relevant leading polynomials “are powers of
+a common linear polynomial in `pi`.”  Moh uses it inside Prop.6.1 to prove the
+floor 1.  It is not a formula recovering `delta^*` from `(M,V,d)`.
