+> “`delta_s=-1` and the logarithmic radius `delta^*_{s-1}` of the minor
+> disc `D^*_{s-1} >= v_s/u_s`.”
+
+With `gamma=theta^(1/u_s)`, it then gives polynomials monic in `pi`, with
+`pi`-degrees
+
+```text
+u_s n/d_s,  u_s(-mu_1)/d_s, ..., u_s(-mu_{s-1})/d_s,
+```
+
+and the stated Jacobian `-(u_s/b) gamma^(v_s-u_s-1)`.  The last display of
+the proof on p.198 prints the exponent in a denominator; the proposition's
+statement and the Appendix-II monomials use the positive exponent.  This is
+the already charged `ERRATUM[PROP63-JAC-SIGN]`, not a new inference here.
+
+`SOURCE-READ`, p.198, Proposition 6.4 adds `u_s=1` and concludes
+
+> “the logarithmic radius `delta^*_{s-1}` of the minor disc
+> `D^*_{s-1} >= v_s/u_s = v_s`.”
